'One complete static bathroom mirror-ledge arrangement, one new scene zero new independent models. The entire qualified six-slot catch-basin soap dish rests at the left of a projecting wall ledge; the entire qualified waisted round-head electric-toothbrush exterior stands separately to its right. Both retain all exact GLB payloads, normals, PBR dictionaries, face assignments and internal hierarchy under unit-scale whole translations only. New scene-only context is a complete rear wall patch with a projecting solid shelf and two returned underside supports, plus a small inset round metallic-PBR mirror area attached above the left side. No prior floor mirror is cut apart, resized or relabelled wall-mounted. No existing prop extracted, cropped, scaled or recoloured; the scene environment is not counted as a new independent mirror or shelf asset. No water, soap, charging, oral-health effect, sanitation, glass-safety, installation, load, reflection-fidelity, physical stability or safety capability. Rigging animation and interaction not made.'
